# Verify before complete — always apply

Before marking the final todo done, telling the user a task is finished, or posting a final
chat or pull request answer: run the procedure in
[`verify-before-complete/SKILL.md`](../skills/verify-before-complete/SKILL.md) — re-read the brief,
verify every requirement against actual produced output, then close with an unprompted self-eval.

## Forbidden

- Completing on intent ("should work") instead of running the skill's verification-per-requirement
  check.
- Marking the last todo done with commits sitting unpushed, or with a blocking gap reclassified as
  deferred just to reach "done."
- Reporting a documented failure, or an actor's own success claim, as done when the brief was to
  make something work.
